## Check 14 — the two former rustup-figure gaps

$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://rustsec.org/packages/rustup.html
404
$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://rustsec.org/packages/time.html
200
$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://rustsec.org/packages/atty.html
200

$ curl -sS -L https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/rustup
HTTP 403 on the unauthenticated default request; the response was not JSON.

# The archived r1 audit recorded the same access condition and used this explicit
# descriptive User-Agent. Retrying the identical endpoint with it is an access-condition
# retry, not a changed query.
$ curl -sS -L -A 'rs-launch-blueprint empirical audit/1.0' https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/rustup | jq '{newest_version: .crate.newest_version, max_stable_version: .crate.max_stable_version, license: .crate.license}'
{
  "newest_version": "0.0.0",
  "max_stable_version": null,
  "license": null
}

# The documented endpoint identifies the placeholder. This companion versions endpoint
# establishes the decision's stronger claim that its only version is yanked.
$ curl -sS -L -A 'rs-launch-blueprint empirical audit/1.0' https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/rustup/versions | jq '[.versions[] | {num, yanked, license, created_at}]'
[
  {
    "num": "0.1.0",
    "yanked": true,
    "license": "MIT",
    "created_at": "2018-03-29T19:59:26.006143Z"
  }
]

$ gh api repos/rust-lang/rustup --jq '{repo: .full_name, license: .license.spdx_id}'
{"license":"Apache-2.0","repo":"rust-lang/rustup"}
$ gh api repos/rust-lang/cargo --jq '{repo: .full_name, license: .license.spdx_id}'
{"license":"Apache-2.0","repo":"rust-lang/cargo"}

